# Web cards member-feed safeguard

## What went wrong (2026-11-24, local ship_tmp only)

Member `web_cards` feeds were rebuilt while only patching
`auth_system.is_premium_user`. Chip lock text comes from
`paywall.is_premium_user` (imported by name). The rebuild baked
"Members only · Join Premium" into the paid feed. Live was fine because
live was never rebuilt that way — same code tree, poisoned **cache**.

## Never do

- Delete warm `web_cards/*.v2.json.gz` without an unlocked replacement ready
- Save a `member` feed that contains "Members only" / "Join Premium" on chips
- Patch only `auth_system.is_premium_user` for member SSR — also patch
  `paywall.is_premium_user` and `NHL77FINAL.is_premium_user`

## Always do

- Refuse to persist locked member feeds (`_payload_has_locked_member_chips`)
- Keep `*.member.ok.v2.json.gz` as the last known-good unlocked member feed
- Keep `*.head10.v2.json.gz` so first 10 cards paint while a full rebuild runs
- Prefer restoring `.ok` over serving a locked member feed
